    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All green \u2014 build succeeds and the test passes. The audit log confirms the behavior: an owner registered on 2026-10-02 now gets `membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M27` (fiscal year ending June 2027 \u2192 FY27), rather than the old `-M26`.\n\n## Summary\n\nMoved every date-derived value to a fiscal-year basis (fiscal year starts 1 July, identified by the calendar year it ends).\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**\n- Added `static int fiscalYear(LocalDate)` \u2014 the single source of truth: a date on/after 1 July of year Y belongs to the fiscal year ending Y+1, otherwise Y.\n- Added `getFiscalYear()` returning `\"FY<YY>\"` (last two digits of the fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted `registrationDate`), so it serializes into the owner response.\n- Changed tenure in `getMembershipPoints()` from a 365-day window to **elapsed fiscal years** (`fiscalYear(today) - fiscalYear(registrationDate) >= 1`), and updated the Javadoc. A fresh owner still has zero tenure.\n- Swapped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import for `Month`.\n\n**`rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipNumber.java`**\n- The membership number's `YY` segment now uses `Owner.fiscalYear(...)` instead of the raw registration year.\n\n**`resources/openapi.yml`** (source for the generated `OwnerDto` the mapper fills by name)\n- Added the `fiscalYear` property to the `Owner` schema.\n- Updated the `membershipNumber` and `membershipPoints` descriptions/examples to reflect the fiscal-year basis.\n\nThe stored `registrationDate` is already business-day-adjusted (set in `BuildOwner` via `RegistrationDates.effective`), so all three values are correctly derived from the adjusted date.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the spec didn't pin the exact tenure threshold or the FY labelling convention. I used the Australian ending-year convention (FY ending 30 June 2027 \u2192 \"FY27\") and treated \"tenured\" as **at least one elapsed fiscal year** (the registration date falling in an earlier fiscal year than today), which preserves the original \"zero tenure for a fresh owner / ~a year earns the bonus\" intent. Both the membership number and `fiscalYear` share the one helper, so they stay consistent. Happy to switch to a starting-year label or a stricter (`>= 2`) threshold if that matches your intended reading.",
