    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the existing conventions in this codebase cleanly:\n\n- `fiscalYear(LocalDate)` is a single public static helper, and all three consumers (`getFiscalYear()`, `getMembershipPoints()`, `AssignMembershipNumber`) route through it \u2014 no duplicated fiscal-year logic. This mirrors the established pattern in `Owner` where static helpers (`regionOf`, `postcodeRangeOf`, `regionOfPostcode`, `identityKey`) are the single source of truth and instance getters delegate to them.\n- `getFiscalYear()` sits directly after the `registrationDate` getter/setter, grouped with the field it derives from, and follows the same \"derived getter returns `null` when the source is absent\" idiom used by `getAgeBand()`, `getTimezone()`, etc.\n- The membership-points tenure change is a minimal, in-place swap of the comparison expression, keeping the method's existing shape; the Javadoc was updated to match.\n- `AssignMembershipNumber` stays a thin one-method function, delegating the year computation to `Owner` rather than growing its own date logic \u2014 consistent with the OfficeFloor function-per-step convention.\n- The OpenAPI schema addition (`fiscalYear`) parallels the surrounding derived read-only fields.\n\nThe small shared `% 100` + two-digit formatting between `getFiscalYear()` and `AssignMembershipNumber` is not worth extracting \u2014 the two produce distinct output formats (`FY27` vs `\u2026-M27`), and the `% 100` form already predates this change in `AssignMembershipNumber`. Logic is in the right unit; nothing is becoming a catch-all.",
